2026-09-27T12:05:49.5204071Z Description:
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5204586Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5205034Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5206092Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5207228Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5207468Z Update Note
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5207830Z ===========
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5208434Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5208828Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5209039Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5209468Z ================
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5209699Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5210010Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5210777Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5211227Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5211409Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5211832Z ====================================
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5214032Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5214291Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5215191Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5215804Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5217325Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5218052Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5218319Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5218996Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5219884Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5220427Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5220866Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5221476Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5221778Z Packages
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5222164Z ========
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5222364Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5223977Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5225747Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5226058Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5226737Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5228555Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5229386Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5242346Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5243356Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5244100Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5244297Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5244883Z ==========================
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5245167Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5246603Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5248392Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5249531Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5251122Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T12:05:49.5251522Z 
